dsh-better-git-worktree: third-party notices
=============================================

## dsh-git-worktree

The composer Worktree switch, the session-list status indicator and the
session-header menu borrow the UX of `dsh-git-worktree`
(https://github.com/wloops/dsh-git-worktree). No code from it is included; this
plugin drops its review/acceptance lifecycle entirely.

## @deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-workspace

Earlier releases of this plugin inlined the client half of
`@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-workspace` into a generated bundle, with a set of
exact-string "seams" applied. That package is MIT licensed:

    @deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-workspace
    Copyright (c) DeepSeek
    MIT License, https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness

This release no longer contains any of it. It adds to the official Workspace UI
through the slot seats that UI declares, and re-registers the official `archive`
entries' component and injected behaviour at runtime (it reads them from the slot
registry; nothing is copied). The attribution is kept because the UX it decorates
and the archive component it reuses are that package's.

Working copies themselves are plain `git init` checkouts reading the source's
objects through an alternate: no third-party code is involved in creating or
managing them.
